---
import study from '../../../corpus/error-study.json';
import { href } from '../lib/data';
const prevented = study.studies.filter(example => example.category === 'rust_typecheck');
---
<div class="error-studies">
  {prevented.map(example => <article class="error-study">
    <h3>{example.title}</h3>
    <p>{example.claim}</p>
    <p class="evidence"><strong>{example.chialisp[0].weak_suite?.length} limited Chialisp tests pass</strong> · a recorded counterexample fails · Rust rejects with <code>{example.rust.compilation.diagnostics.map(item => item.code).join(', ')}</code>.</p>
  </article>)}
</div>
<p class="source-note">These are precise source-type and name guarantees under the shown APIs. The missing-cap control still compiles in Rust: type checking does not establish authorization or conservation. Rue’s observed protections are recorded separately.</p>
<p><a href={href('verification/error-study/')}>Read the failing sources, missed inputs, actual diagnostics, and remaining mistakes →</a></p>
<style>
  .error-studies { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin-block: 1.4rem; }
  .error-study { border: 1px solid var(--oxide-line); padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem; border-radius: 5px; }
  h3 { font-size: 1rem; margin: 0 0 .6rem; }
  p { font-size: .83rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .evidence { font-size: .73rem; color: var(--sl-color-gray-2); }
  @media (max-width: 44rem) { .error-studies { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
